title: Events
act: Mine
location: Gallery
scenario: The collapse
when: once
when: here() == "Gallery"
---
The old gallery. Timbers lie across the floor like dropped matches, and the air is thick with dust. #line:Events.cb2a808c_0100
Three ways lead on into the dark: the old shaft, the flooded gallery, and the long way round. #line:Events.cb2a808c_0200
===

title: Events
act: Mine
location: Deep
scenario: The lights
when: once
when: here() == "Deep" and $oil > 0
---
The deep level. A seam of rock glows green along the far wall, and under it, carvings, line after line of them. #line:Events.1f25ef16_0100
The lantern folk. Not ghosts. A border, written in stone. #line:Events.1f25ef16_0200
===

title: Events
act: Mine
location: Deep
scenario: The collapse
quest: jory
when: once
when: here() == "Deep" and $oil <= 0 and $quest_jory == QuestState.Active
---
// The long way took the last of the oil: the cartographer reaches the deep level in the dark.
Your lamp gutters and goes out. The dark is total. #line:Events.4a46c54a_0100
Somewhere close, a man coughs. You call, and he calls back, but in the dark the voice comes from everywhere at once. #line:Events.4a46c54a_0200
You feel your way back along the wall to the lift, and ride it up. #line:Events.4a46c54a_0300
<<set $quest_jory to QuestState.Failed>>
<<quest_changed jory>>
<<go DeepLift>>
===

title: OldShaft
act: Mine
location: Gallery
scenario: The collapse
quest: jory
---
<<if has_item("rope")>>
    You tie Bram's old rope to a timber and climb down the shaft, hand over hand. #line:OldShaft_0100
    <<if $way == WayDown.None>>
        <<set $way to WayDown.Rope>>
    <<endif>>
    <<go OldShaft>>
<<else>>
    The old shaft drops straight into the dark. Without a rope, it is a grave. #line:OldShaft_0200
<<endif>>
===

title: FloodedPassage
act: Mine
location: Gallery
scenario: The collapse
quest: jory
---
<<if has_item("remedy")>>
    You drink Nan's remedy. It burns all the way down, and then you are warm, warm enough for black water. #line:FloodedPassage_0100
    <<take remedy>>
    <<go FloodedPassage>>
<<else>>
    The flooded gallery is black and still. You put a hand in the water and your fingers go numb at once. #line:FloodedPassage_0200
    Not without something against the cold. #line:FloodedPassage_0300
<<endif>>
===

title: FloodedOn
act: Mine
location: Flooded
scenario: The collapse
quest: jory
when: $way == WayDown.None
---
You wade on, chest-deep, holding the lamp over your head, until the floor rises under your feet. #line:FloodedOn.dd8dfe76_0100
<<set $way to WayDown.Flooded>>
<<go FloodedOn>>
===

title: LongWay
act: Mine
location: Gallery
scenario: The collapse
quest: jory
---
// The long way burns a measure of oil more: with none left after it, the cartographer arrives in the dark.
<<if $oil <= 0>>
    The long way winds off into the dark. Without oil, you would never come back. #line:LongWay_0100
<<else>>
    <<set $oil to $oil - 1>>
    <<if $oil > 0>>
        The long way winds down and down, through galleries nobody has walked in forty years. Your lamp burns low. #line:LongWay_0200
    <<else>>
        The long way winds down and down. Halfway, your lamp begins to gutter. #line:LongWay_0300
    <<endif>>
    <<if $way == WayDown.None>>
        <<set $way to WayDown.Long>>
    <<endif>>
    <<go LongWay>>
<<endif>>
===

title: Corvin
act: Mine
location: Gallery
scenario: The follower
quest: corvin
when: here() == "Gallery" and $corvin_in_mine
when: $corvin_fate == CorvinFate.Unmet
---
// The fifth fork: the steward, pinned under a timber in the gallery.
Corvin is on the floor of the gallery, a timber across his legs, his lamp broken beside him. #line:Corvin.0c7a3922_0100
<<if $offer == Offer.Proof>>
    Corvin: You. With my letter in your pocket. Come to watch? #mood:angry #line:Corvin.0c7a3922_0200_Corvin
<<elseif $offer == Offer.Refused>>
    Corvin: The honest cartographer. Help me, or go away. #mood:angry #line:Corvin.0c7a3922_0300_Corvin
<<else>>
    Corvin: Thank the saints. Get this off me. #line:Corvin.0c7a3922_0400_Corvin
<<endif>>
Corvin: I came to see the carvings before you did. That's all. A steward's curiosity. #line:Corvin.0c7a3922_0500_Corvin
A notebook sticks out of his coat. You can see a border drawn in it, and the same border copied again, older-looking each time. #line:Corvin.0c7a3922_0600
-> Lift the timber. <<if $oil > 0>> #line:Corvin.0c7a3922_0700
    It takes a long time, and your lamp burns low while you work. But the timber moves. #line:Corvin.0c7a3922_0800
    <<set $oil to $oil - 1>>
    <<set $corvin_fate to CorvinFate.Helped>>
    Corvin: I won't forget this. I don't say that often. #line:Corvin.0c7a3922_0900_Corvin
    <<set $corvin_in_mine to false>>
-> Lift the timber, and take the notebook while he is dazed. <<if $oil > 0>> #line:Corvin.0c7a3922_1000
    You free him, and while he gasps on the floor, the notebook goes into your coat. #line:Corvin.0c7a3922_1100
    <<set $oil to $oil - 1>>
    <<set $corvin_fate to CorvinFate.Robbed>>
    <<give notebook>>
    <<set $corvin_in_mine to false>>
    Corvin: My thanks. And my notebook? No? It must have fallen. #mood:angry #line:Corvin.0c7a3922_1200_Corvin
-> Leave him for the miners. #line:Corvin.0c7a3922_1300
    <<set $corvin_fate to CorvinFate.Left>>
    Corvin: You can't leave me here! Cartographer! #mood:angry #line:Corvin.0c7a3922_1400_Corvin
    The miners will dig him out, in a day or two. After the fair. #line:Corvin.0c7a3922_1500
<<set $quest_corvin to QuestState.Succeeded>>
<<quest_changed corvin>>
===

title: Corvin
act: Mine
location: Gallery
scenario: The follower
when: here() == "Gallery" and $corvin_in_mine
when: $corvin_fate == CorvinFate.Left
---
Corvin says nothing now. He is saving his breath for the miners. #line:Corvin.08bf5546_0100
===

title: Jory
act: Mine
location: Deep
scenario: The collapse
quest: jory
when: $quest_jory == QuestState.Active and $oil > 0
---
Jory: A light! Over here! My leg's caught in the rails. #line:Jory.c932b1e8_0100_Jory
You work his foot free. He can walk, slowly. #line:Jory.c932b1e8_0200
Jory: I followed the green light down. Thought it was the lantern folk come to take me. It's only a wall. Look at it. #line:Jory.c932b1e8_0300_Jory
<<set $jory_found to true>>
<<set $quest_jory to QuestState.Succeeded>>
<<quest_changed jory>>
<<walk Jory DeepLift>>
Jory: I'll wait at the lift. Don't be long. The oil won't be. #line:Jory.c932b1e8_0400_Jory
===

title: Jory
act: Mine
location: Deep
scenario: The collapse
when: $jory_found
---
=> Jory: At the lift when you're ready. #line:Jory.f62c36a4_0100_Jory
=> Jory: My mother will kill me. Then she'll feed me. #line:Jory.f62c36a4_0200_Jory
=> Jory: The carvings go on for twenty paces. I counted them, in the dark, by hand. #line:Jory.f62c36a4_0300_Jory
===

title: Carvings
act: Mine
location: Deep
scenario: The lights
quest: carvings
when: $quest_carvings == QuestState.Active
---
<<if $oil <= 0>>
    It is too dark to see the carvings, let alone copy them. #line:Carvings.0e0873aa_0100
<<else>>
    You copy the carvings into the map, line by line. A mason's mark at each end: a circle with a line through it. #line:Carvings.0e0873aa_0200
    <<if $quest_page == QuestState.Succeeded>>
        They match the charter's page. From the bridge stone, north under the hill, to the abbey's well. The true border. #line:Carvings.0e0873aa_0300
    <<else>>
        A border, clearly. Where it runs above ground, you can only guess, but the stones by the bridge carry the same mark. #line:Carvings.0e0873aa_0400
    <<endif>>
    <<survey carvings>>
    <<set $carvings_copied to true>>
    <<set $quest_carvings to QuestState.Succeeded>>
    <<quest_changed carvings>>
<<endif>>
===

title: Carvings
act: All
location: Deep
scenario: The lights
when: $quest_carvings != QuestState.Active
---
The carvings glow faintly in the green light. They are on your map now, or lost to it. #line:Carvings.ce2153f0_0100
===

title: DeepLift
act: Mine
location: Deep
scenario: The lights
when: $quest_carvings == QuestState.Active and $oil > 0
---
The carvings are not on your map yet. Go up anyway? #line:DeepLift.55846690_0100
-> Go up. #line:DeepLift.55846690_0200
    <<go DeepLift>>
-> Stay. #line:DeepLift.55846690_0300
===
